(376215, 31857, 4967, '<td valign="top">Hehehe... this is one great movie... I loved it, watched in on the bus while we were touring around Australia.  Where''s the huge flowing skirts though... a little tame for that movie don''t you think ;-)  I like the expressions on their faces though.</td>', 'Hehehe... this is one great movie... I loved it, watched in on the bus while we were touring around Australia.  Where''s the huge flowing skirts though... a little tame for that movie don''t you think ;-)  I like the expressions on their faces though.', '2003-08-04 11:09:06.000000', NULL, 1),
(376250, 31778, 7086, '<td valign="top">My voting criteria for this challenge are:<br/> <br/>1. Did you capture a scene from the movie (as the challenge brief states) or did you enter a picture and fit a title to it.<br/>2. How close a rendition is your image to the movie.<br/>3. How does the image stand up in its own right.<br/> <br/>In this case:<br/> <br/>1. I suppose it''s possible that you can claim this is a scene from the movie, I don''t remember it though.<br/>2. NA. <br/>3. This is a very detailed shot and the different contrasts are well captured. Not the type of image I''d go for but I can see it in a gun magazine or catalogue.<br/> <br/>Overall a good picture which does not really meet the challenge. 4</td>', 'My voting criteria for this challenge are: 1. Did you capture a scene from the movie (as the challenge brief states) or did you enter a picture and fit a title to it.2. How close a rendition is your image to the movie.3. How does the image stand up in its own right. In this case: 1. I suppose it''s possible that you can claim this is a scene from the movie, I don''t remember it though.2. NA. 3. This is a very detailed shot and the different contrasts are well captured. Not the type of image I''d go for but I can see it in a gun magazine or catalogue. Overall a good picture which does not really meet the challenge. 4', '2003-08-04 11:35:20.000000', NULL, 1),
(376261, 31834, 7086, '<td valign="top">My voting criteria for this challenge are:<br/> <br/>1. Did you capture a scene from the movie (as the challenge brief states) or did you enter a picture and fit a title to it.<br/>2. How close a rendition is your image to the movie.<br/>3. How does the image stand up in its own right.<br/> <br/>In this case:<br/> <br/>1. Pretty obvious that you shot this specifically for the challenge.<br/>2. I''d not even heard of this movie until I saw your entry. Just had a look at the film web-site and from what I understand of the plot this must sum up some of the feeling of the film. <br/>3. Would this image stand up in its own right? Yes, it shows loss and definitely has an emotional impact.<br/> <br/>Overall a good picture which, I guess, meets the challenge. 10</td>', 'My voting criteria for this challenge are: 1. Did you capture a scene from the movie (as the challenge brief states) or did you enter a picture and fit a title to it.2. How close a rendition is your image to the movie.3. How does the image stand up in its own right. In this case: 1. Pretty obvious that you shot this specifically for the challenge.2. I''d not even heard of this movie until I saw your entry. Just had a look at the film web-site and from what I understand of the plot this must sum up some of the feeling of the film. 3. Would this image stand up in its own right? Yes, it shows loss and definitely has an emotional impact. Overall a good picture which, I guess, meets the challenge. 10', '2003-08-04 11:43:38.000000', NULL, 1),
(376262, 31525, 6651, '<td valign="top">Crossing my eyes hurts, but the imagery is great</td>', 'Crossing my eyes hurts, but the imagery is great', '2003-08-04 11:43:59.000000', NULL, 1),
(376265, 31787, 7086, '<td valign="top">My voting criteria for this challenge are:<br/> <br/>1. Did you capture a scene from the movie (as the challenge brief states) or did you enter a picture and fit a title to it.<br/>2. How close a rendition is your image to the movie.<br/>3. How does the image stand up in its own right.<br/> <br/>In this case:<br/> <br/>1. OK it''s a camel and there were camels in the film, however I feel that you could have picked any arabian set film and claimed a fit.<br/>2. NA. <br/>3. As animal pictures go not the best. The over-exposure on the head is really distracting and the body lacks definition.<br/> <br/>4</td>', 'My voting criteria for this challenge are: 1. Did you capture a scene from the movie (as the challenge brief states) or did you enter a picture and fit a title to it.2. How close a rendition is your image to the movie.3. How does the image stand up in its own right. In this case: 1. OK it''s a camel and there were camels in the film, however I feel that you could have picked any arabian set film and claimed a fit.2. NA. 3. As animal pictures go not the best. The over-exposure on the head is really distracting and the body lacks definition. 4', '2003-08-04 11:47:42.000000', NULL, 1),
