(382793, 31768, 7086, '<td valign="top">My voting criteria for this challenge are:<br/> <br/>1. Did you capture a scene from the movie (as the challenge brief states) or did you enter a picture and fit a title to it.<br/>2. How close a rendition is your image to the movie.<br/>3. How does the image stand up in its own right.<br/> <br/>In this case:<br/> <br/>1. Pretty obvious that you shot this specifically for the challenge.<br/>2. Almost spot on. I guess this is the scene most people remember, even those who haven''t seen the film will know it. You''ve captured an image that screams its title without being titled. <br/>3. Would this image stand up in its own right? Difficult to say as it''s so closely tied to the film. Beginners should be told to look at this image as a photographic exercise in lighting and contrast.<br/> <br/>Superb image. 10</td>', 'My voting criteria for this challenge are: 1. Did you capture a scene from the movie (as the challenge brief states) or did you enter a picture and fit a title to it.2. How close a rendition is your image to the movie.3. How does the image stand up in its own right. In this case: 1. Pretty obvious that you shot this specifically for the challenge.2. Almost spot on. I guess this is the scene most people remember, even those who haven''t seen the film will know it. You''ve captured an image that screams its title without being titled. 3. Would this image stand up in its own right? Difficult to say as it''s so closely tied to the film. Beginners should be told to look at this image as a photographic exercise in lighting and contrast. Superb image. 10', '2003-08-09 17:04:40.000000', NULL, 1),
(382851, 30912, 280, '<td valign="top">Havent seen the film (not sure I want to :-), but in my humble opinion your photo is great, I love the models poses and the shadow of the arm/needle on the wall. My only slight criticisms are; the glove and mask look a tad over exposed. Also the object, in the bottom right of the frame slightly obscuring the victims face, looks a little out of place. Apart from that it is a cracking photo. Good luck... Tom.</td>', 'Havent seen the film (not sure I want to :-), but in my humble opinion your photo is great, I love the models poses and the shadow of the arm/needle on the wall. My only slight criticisms are; the glove and mask look a tad over exposed. Also the object, in the bottom right of the frame slightly obscuring the victims face, looks a little out of place. Apart from that it is a cracking photo. Good luck... Tom.', '2003-08-09 18:50:12.000000', NULL, 1),
