(383682, 31836, 5585, '<td valign="top">Hi .. Thanks for everyones comments on my picture in the Movie Challenge..the Ship is atop of a Bar called Pirates Cove.in the Place I work... River Palms Hotel and Casino... Laughlin, Nevada.. It is Approx. 60 ft...long... and a couple stories high.the pic was cropped resized saturated to show night...Sharpened a hair..and I think that was about itas for the subjectthe ship is animated .. with a Pirate a Wench.. a couple of Parrots.and they are full of song .and talk movement looks about as good as Disney..and I think it adds to the experience of visiting the CasinoIf I can ..I will  show everyone the real picture ..one of the other Challenge entries At Work has a portion of the bar.thank you all again</td>', 'Hi .. Thanks for everyones comments on my picture in the Movie Challenge..the Ship is atop of a Bar called Pirates Cove.in the Place I work... River Palms Hotel and Casino... Laughlin, Nevada.. It is Approx. 60 ft...long... and a couple stories high.the pic was cropped resized saturated to show night...Sharpened a hair..and I think that was about itas for the subjectthe ship is animated .. with a Pirate a Wench.. a couple of Parrots.and they are full of song .and talk movement looks about as good as Disney..and I think it adds to the experience of visiting the CasinoIf I can ..I will  show everyone the real picture ..one of the other Challenge entries At Work has a portion of the bar.thank you all again', '2003-08-11 01:40:49.000000', NULL, 0),
(383687, 31842, 1, '<td valign="top">Wonderful shot.. the background is a bit odd, but still wonderful.</td>', 'Wonderful shot.. the background is a bit odd, but still wonderful.', '2003-08-11 01:44:19.000000', NULL, 0),
(383693, 31804, 4967, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club<br/> <br/>Hi OneSweetSin, I''d guessed this was yours during voting... I thought I''d seen this little boy in your photos before :-)  <br/> <br/>First off, it definitely fits the challenge.  Very cute.  I loved home alone!  It''s amazing to me that McCaulley Culkin is already grown and married, we''re similar ages!  Anyway, good job choosing your subject for the photo.<br/> <br/>The lighting here leaves a lot to be desired.. it is very flat and straightforward, and doesn''t really do a lot for the photo.  He looks like he has a bluish tint to him, I know that part of it is from the koolaid (?)  but I''m sure he didn''t get it on his forehead.  Hehehe... <br/> <br/>I like your composition... filling the frame was nicely done here and it helped with no distractions surrounding the kid.  <br/> <br/>This looks quite a bit like a snapshot, but it''s not a big deal... I would try and work on getting better lighting for sure.  Play around with lighting... doing this outdoors without a flash might have been a good thing.<br/> <br/>Good luck in the future!<br/> <br/>-Talya</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club Hi OneSweetSin, I''d guessed this was yours during voting... I thought I''d seen this little boy in your photos before :-)   First off, it definitely fits the challenge.  Very cute.  I loved home alone!  It''s amazing to me that McCaulley Culkin is already grown and married, we''re similar ages!  Anyway, good job choosing your subject for the photo. The lighting here leaves a lot to be desired.. it is very flat and straightforward, and doesn''t really do a lot for the photo.  He looks like he has a bluish tint to him, I know that part of it is from the koolaid (?)  but I''m sure he didn''t get it on his forehead.  Hehehe...  I like your composition... filling the frame was nicely done here and it helped with no distractions surrounding the kid.   This looks quite a bit like a snapshot, but it''s not a big deal... I would try and work on getting better lighting for sure.  Play around with lighting... doing this outdoors without a flash might have been a good thing. Good luck in the future! -Talya', '2003-08-11 01:48:56.000000', NULL, 0),
